{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1008030-after-life-not-undeath","id":1008030,"title":"After Life, Not Undeath","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-25T04:57:45-08:00","id":1008030,"title":"After Life, Not Undeath","content":"So as I understand it, neither the Bargain nor the Geist heal a Sin-Eater at all. Does this then mean that there is a very large downtime, or recuperation period after the Bargain? Would someone crushed under debris need to heal in a hospital for months? Would someone immolated need to recover for years? Sorry, I'm very new and very fuzzy with the rules. Any clarification or a point in the right direction in the book would very welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10919-omepraiser","name":"OmePraiser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T05:14:51-08:00","id":1008031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OmePraiser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1008030-after-life-not-undeath#post1008030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So as I understand it, neither the Bargain nor the Geist heal a Sin-Eater at all. Does this then mean that there is a very large downtime, or recuperation period after the Bargain? Would someone crushed under debris need to heal in a hospital for months? Would someone immolated need to recover for years? Sorry, I'm very new and very fuzzy with the rules. Any clarification or a point in the right direction in the book would very welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, the Bargain staves off death and speeds healing, to a degree, although it's not instant, nor does it necessarily return complete functionality. The Geist wants to live vicariously, after all, and it's not much of a life trapped in a hospital bed. I'm not entirely certain on the actual process of the thing, though, nor on the exact mechanics. Probably something to do with the plasm suffusing the Sin-Eater's body and blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T11:21:28-08:00","id":1008216,"title":"","content":"It does heal them... most of the time anyway. It seems like you can have your bones heal from being crushed ridiculously quick and you could heal burns ridiculously quick, but if you had hand cut off, then that wont regrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T11:36:15-08:00","id":1008221,"title":"","content":"That's what confuses me. The book clarifies that &quot;the Bargain doesn't heal the Sin-Eater's wounds&quot;, &quot;Geists cannot restore life or heal a living mortal&quot; and &quot;whatever injures brought the Sin-Eater to the brink of death linger&quot;. The only healing it notes is normal human recovery. So basically the trauma needs to be enough to kill someone but in a way that doesn't significantly damage the body otherwise the Geist doesn't want you? If your character is the victim of an animal mauling ala The Prey, does that mean said character comes back but horribly, permanently disfigured? Wouldn't you be missing huge chunks of flesh and organs? The only impression I'm getting from the text is that you end up a bedridden, disfigured lump of pain until you heal naturally. Unless you pick a method of death that's very self-contained I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10919-omepraiser","name":"OmePraiser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:47:00-08:00","id":1008276,"title":"","content":"I am far from a Geist expert, but my understanding is that coming back a Bound is supposed to look, from an outside perspective, like surviving a near-death experience. That doesn't really work if your recovery is supernaturally fast. So, yeah, the Geist might heal you to the point where the experience doesn't kill you, but the injuries still have to heal naturally otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-25-2016, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:48:35-08:00","id":1008279,"title":"","content":"That does raise an interesting point though, that a lot of Prey and Maimed should probably have injury-induced disabilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T17:51:37-08:00","id":1008343,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that while not <i>all</i> damage is recovered from, the majority of it is recovered, even to the point that scars are minimal. Sin Eaters tend not to come out of the bargain with permanent disabilities from what I've seen - even people who died from biological issues, like an allergic reaction, cancer or chocking from their own mucus, come back relatively no worse for wear. That said, I do remember one of the pre-made characters died by falling off a horse, and that he has a pop in his neck when he moves it a certain way, and a girl who died via copper poisoning found that her hair remained green afterwards, so quirks do remain.<br /> <br /> I dunno, I suppose it's all up to the storyteller and players to work out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:45:26-08:00","id":1010504,"title":"","content":"I believe that some examples of the damage lingering from the death of the Sin-Eater can be found on the Balance of Shadows thread. <br /> <br /> Now as I am currently working on a Sin-Eater/Beast chronicle this is my ruling on the Agreement and effects on the body.<br /> 1. The damage done will heal, not quickly but full recovery will be made short of any amputations.<br /> 2. If a player chooses and I stress chooses their maybe lingering effects brought on by beginning play before complete recovery. Example from the characters that have been created. Neil Morgan was chosen by Shards of Glass a human shaped collection of glass shards when he died by a glass shard from a broken window. The window cut him deeply in several places including his leg. This wound was the one that ended his life. If the person playing Neil decides that he wanted to push his character out of therapy early I would probably rule a he has a distinct limp, needs a cane, and has a penalty applied to movement and dexterity based actions. This could then be bought off over time as the wound fully heals. <br /> 3. The other Sin-Eater starved to death sitting in front of a computer monitor. This character to start looks unhealthy, but as part of the new life is eating a lot more so I really don't think any kind of lingering effect is valid.<br /> <br /> As Taidragon said this really is something that should be decided based on individual players and storytellers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T22:14:56-08:00","id":1010517,"title":"","content":"Within 2E mechanics, you can say that a freshly resurrected Bound has a Condition reflecting his original cause of death, granting penalties to certain Skills and Attributes, that resolve after time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T21:21:26-08:00","id":1014141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1008030-after-life-not-undeath?p=1010517#post1010517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Within 2E mechanics, you can say that a freshly resurrected Bound has a Condition reflecting his original cause of death, granting penalties to certain Skills and Attributes, that resolve after time.</div> </div> </div> </div>One way to handle it:<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters heal cleanly (they don't need surgery to remove Persistent conditions that normally require it), and can walk off anything short of Lethal in record time. Beyond that (and their immunity to falling unconscious), they get hurt just like mortals. The bargain does the <i>bare minimum</i> necessary for you to be up and breathing again - and if you'd be left in a state that's useless for vicarious living, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/164385-body-hopping-resurrection\">a suitable new vacancy just opened up</a>...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T08:16:54-08:00","id":1014319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1008030-after-life-not-undeath?p=1014141#post1014141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One way to handle it:<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters heal cleanly (they don't need surgery to remove Persistent conditions that normally require it), and can walk off anything short of Lethal in record time. Beyond that (and their immunity to falling unconscious), they get hurt just like mortals. The bargain does the <i>bare minimum</i> necessary for you to be up and breathing again - and if you'd be left in a state that's useless for vicarious living, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/164385-body-hopping-resurrection\">a suitable new vacancy just opened up</a>...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, that body-hopping is brilliant. It kinda reminds me of the Claiming rules - perhaps one way of subtly telling that no, the Bound are not just humans with a death-god stapled on to them, but a half-ghost thing themselves now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T10:15:11-08:00","id":1014355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1008030-after-life-not-undeath?p=1014319#post1014319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooh, that body-hopping is brilliant. It kinda reminds me of the Claiming rules - perhaps one way of subtly telling that no, the Bound are not just humans with a death-god stapled on to them, but a half-ghost thing themselves now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything we touch touches in return, no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T03:29:27-08:00","id":1025817,"title":"","content":"I would say that Geist heals you half time quicker and you get starting Condition - if you will have full Lethal, it still be like 7 days till your original recovery, instead of 14 in normal pace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T06:36:23-08:00","id":1025896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1008030-after-life-not-undeath?p=1025817#post1025817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that Geist heals you half time quicker and you get starting Condition - if you will have full Lethal, it still be like 7 days till your original recovery, instead of 14 in normal pace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like this?<br /> <br /> <b>New Condition: Fresh Bargain</b><br /> You have just made a Bargain with a geist, becoming Bound to it. Being newly resurrected has its perks. You are alive, for one, and all your healing times are halved. Any Persistent Conditions related to bodily damage are resolved without Beats. On the other hand, the shock of death requires some adjustment time to recover from. You suffer a -2 penalty to any rolls involving Resolve, Stamina, or Composure. <br /> <b>Resolution</b>: The Bound is restored to full health, and afterwards spends Experience on any Bound-specific trait, ability or Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T07:02:27-08:00","id":1025921,"title":"","content":"<b>Hermit</b>, so 2 Conditions - one of your original idea, related to death source, and second that let you heal at half time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T07:30:21-08:00","id":1025934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1008030-after-life-not-undeath?p=1025921#post1025921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hermit</b>, so 2 Conditions - one of your original idea, related to death source, and second that let you heal at half time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Then...<br /> <br /> <b>New Condition: Fresh Bargain</b><br /> You have just made a Bargain with a geist, becoming Bound to it. Being newly resurrected has its perks. You are alive, for one, and all your healing times are halved. Any Persistent Conditions related to bodily damage are resolved without Beats. On the other hand, the shock of death requires some adjustment time to recover from. You lose all Willpower points upon acquiring this Condition, which can be normally recovered.<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: The Bound is restored to full physical and mental health, and afterwards spends Experience on any Bound-specific trait, ability or Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>New Condition: Deathmark</b><br /> You have just been initiated into the Thresholds of death that the dead abide by, and the Horsemen have marked you as their own. This Condition is acquired automatically when the Fresh Bargain Condition is imposed. You suffer different penalties depending on your Threshold, as the shadow of death lingers still above you.<br /> The Forgotten have been blindsided by death and are still dazed by it, suffering a -2 penalty to Wits and Dexterity.<br /> The Prey know that the dangers of the wild still lurk outside, suffering a -2 penalty to Stamina and Composure.<br /> The Torn had their muscles and bones ripped apart violenty, suffering a -2 penalty to Strength and Stamina.<br /> The Stricken were robbed of their finer faculties due to wasting, suffering a -2 penalty to Dexterity and Stamina.<br /> The Silent wallow still in the dark depths, suffering a -2 penalty to Resolve and Presence.<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Automatically resolved together with the Fresh Bargain Condition.<br /> <br /> Changed the first one's effects a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}